<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henri Gouraud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1867">1867</a>–<a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henri Gouraud was a French general who served in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, capturing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samori-ture">Samori Ture</a> in 1898 and conquering the Adrar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a> in 1909, and later commanded at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallipoli">Gallipoli</a> and on the Western Front. As French High Commissioner in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> from 1919 to 1923 he defeated Faisal's Arab Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> at Maysalun in 1920, proclaimed Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a> and divided Syria into the states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> and others.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henri-gouraud.jpg" alt="Henri Gouraud" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Auguste Léon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Proprieted%27AlbertKahn-Boulogne-FranceLeGeneralHenriGouraud_A19033.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>French forces under <b>Henri Gouraud</b> occupied Atar in 1909, overcoming resistance encouraged by the scholar Ma al-Aynayn.</blockquote><a href="/state/emirate-of-adrar">Emirate of Adrar</a></li><li><blockquote>After Coppolani's assassination in 1905, military campaigns, including <b>Henri Gouraud's</b> conquest of the Emirate of Adrar in 1909, extended control northward.</blockquote><a href="/state/french-mauritania">French Mauritania</a></li><li><blockquote>On 1 September 1920 General <b>Henri Gouraud</b> proclaimed the State of Greater Lebanon in Beirut.</blockquote><a href="/state/greater-lebanon">Greater Lebanon</a></li><li><blockquote>Following the defeat of the Arab Kingdom of Syria, the French high commissioner <b>Henri Gouraud</b> created the State of Aleppo in September 1920.</blockquote><a href="/state/state-of-aleppo">State of Aleppo</a></li><li><blockquote>After defeating the Arab Kingdom of Syria at Maysalun in July 1920, the French high commissioner <b>Henri Gouraud</b> divided Syria into several states to weaken Arab nationalism.</blockquote><a href="/state/state-of-damascus">State of Damascus</a></li><li><blockquote>In June 1922 the French high commissioner <b>Henri Gouraud</b> united the State of Damascus, the State of Aleppo and the Alawite State in a federation, a partial response to nationalist demands for unity.</blockquote><a href="/state/syrian-federation">Syrian Federation</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in 7th arrondissement of Paris, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. Died in 7th arrondissement of Paris, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=48.86,2.31&amp;year=1918" aria-label="7th arrondissement of Paris on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4603 458 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Henri Gouraud"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5053 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5053 728h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=48.86,2.31&amp;year=1918">What was here in 1918? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
